{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>On the hems, etc.</b> From here I infer that the truth is as those who hold that the bells were in a row with the pomegranates and not actually inside them, for the verse first stated the placing of the pomegranates on the hems of the robe, and afterward it stated the making of the bells on their own, ״וַיִּתְּנוּ אוֹתָם תּוֹךְ הָרִמּוֹנִים״. And now, if the bell were actually inside the pomegranate, why did the verse need to say ״עַל שׁוּלֵי״ when it had already stated beforehand that the pomegranates were on the hems of the robe? This depends on this. And I am astonished at Ramban that he turned away from this approach, and what he settled on — that he did not place the pomegranate on the robe until he had placed the bell inside it — the verse states the opposite of this. And from what he said, that for this reason it repeated saying ״בְּתוֹךְ הָרִמּוֹנִים״ twice, it is difficult: why did the verse first give the command to place the pomegranates on the hems of the robe before making the bells, so that it would need to go back and say twice ״בְּתוֹךְ הָרִמּוֹנִים״ to include that he should put them in beforehand? And the simple explanation is that the Rav did not examine precisely, in accordance with the habit of his holy inquiry."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:14.412410682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}